{"resourceIdentifier":"1794","resourceName":"Interwaste Landfill gas Grouped Project","description":"This project description contains information about both the proposed Grouped Project “Interwaste landfill gas Grouped Project” as well as the first project activity instance at FG Landfill.The party responsible (the Project Proponent) for the Grouped Project and the first project activity instance is Interwaste Holdings Limited. Interwaste has developed a municipal waste landfill gas recovery project and is looking towards producing compressed biogas fuel that can be supplied in to external customers with the distribution in trucks. The project instance is located at the Interwaste FG landfill site. This site is located next to Olifantsfontein road, Tembisa, in Midrand, in the province of Gauteng, Republic of South Africa (RSA).The Grouped Project proposed in this project description allows for the following project activity types:• The installation of a new LFG capture system in an existing or new (Greenfield) SWDS where no LFG capture system was or would have been installed prior to the implementation of the project activity.• Flaring the LFG and/or use in supplying the LFG to consumers using trucks and/or for electricity generations.Hereinafter the first project activity instance of this Grouped Project will be referred to as ‘Project 1’ throughout the document. Interwaste’s FG Landfill Gas Project (project 1) consists of landfill gas recovery from horizontal and vertical gas collection systems at the FG Landfill site. The recovered gas will be processed in a gas cleaning and upgrading facility to a compressed biogas fuel which will be used by external customers, the excess gas will be flared. The technology to be installed as part of the gas cleaning facility is an aerodynamic separation process (ASP) and a pressure swing adsorption (PSA) plant, in addition an enclosed low height flare will be installed.Greenhouse gas emission reductions for Project 1 will be achieved by the combustion of recovered methane contained in landfill gas that would otherwise be emitted to the atmosphere, and/or from the production of compressed biogas (CBG) and its use thereof to displace natural gas. Prior to project implementation the site was a landfill site which included no gas recovery system nor a gas flaring system, thus the baseline scenario is the venting of landfill gas to the atmosphere. The landfill site started collecting and handling waste in 2008.The estimated annual average emission reduction saving for this Project 1 is 37,633 tCO2e and total GHG emission reductions and removals over the lifetime of the crediting periods are 413,965 tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":-25.958500,"longitude":28.181472},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1794"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Gauteng Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Interwaste (Pty) Ltd"},{"type":"string","value":"Tamil Nadu, India"},{"type":"string","value":"www.vvdindia.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1794"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"41396"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0001"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Carbon Check (Pty) Ltd"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"06/04/2020"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 28/10/2016 - 27/10/2026"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","docume